00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:29.000
movies in the suburbs and the city simultaneously. But with just a single screen in most theaters playing two movies meant half as many show times for each one, which led to the next logical step, creating more screens. You had the single screens, and then you had the cutting up of the single screens. So you had these terrible configurations, these bowling alley type auditoriums that resulted from the slicing up of existing movie theaters.
电影。但大多数电影院只有一个放映厅，放映两部电影意味着每部电影的场次减半，这导致了下一个合乎逻辑的步骤：增加放映厅。你有了单厅，然后你有了对单厅的切割。所以你有了这些糟糕的布局，这些保龄球馆式的放映厅，这是对现有电影院进行切割的结果。

