Ted Mundorf's enormous single screen was carved into two, and then four long, narrow auditoriums. And here and there, some little four and six plexus were built, now that there were enough films to sustain them. But as movie going became a less exclusive experience, it became a less exclusive experience. No more tuxedos. As the 70s rolled into the 80s, theaters went from swanky to sticky. Any coke that ever spilled there is still there today. And this cramped, grungy, sort of top floor of the mall movie experience was keeping people away. Ticket sales dropped 15% in the mid-80s.
泰德·蒙多夫巨大的单厅被分割成两个，然后是四个又长又窄的放映厅。到处都建了一些小型的四厅和六厅影院，因为现在有足够的电影来维持它们了。但随着看电影变成了一种不那么独特的体验，它也变得不那么排他了。不再有燕尾服了。随着70年代进入80年代，电影院从时髦变得黏糊糊的。任何曾经洒在那里的可乐至今仍在那里。这种拥挤、肮脏、位于购物中心顶层的电影体验让人们望而却步。80年代中期，门票销售额下降了15%。

