He realized upgrading theaters and offering people more choices was the only way forward. He'd been to Belgium and seen a huge cinema with 25 screens. So he comes back from this trip. He says, this is the future. This is what we have to do. The finance team ran the numbers and said, no, this is a terrible idea. You will never sell enough tickets and popcorn to afford this thing. Increase rents, increase construction cost, and it just didn't work. The math didn't work.
他意识到升级电影院并为人们提供更多选择是唯一的出路。他去过比利时，看到了一家拥有25个放映厅的巨大电影院。所以他从这次旅行回来后说，这就是未来。这就是我们必须做的。财务团队计算了数字后说，不，这是一个糟糕的主意。你永远卖不出足够的电影票和爆米花来负担这个东西。租金增加，建筑成本增加，这根本行不通。数学上算不过来。

