I mean, it was there was a lot of people there and at two o'clock in the morning, if you can believe that for a movie. EMC expected the grand to attract 800,000 visitors in its first year. They got three million. By this point, Ted Mundorf, the guy who used to work as an usher back in the 60s, was film buyer at a theater company in LA. Naturally, he kept an eye on the competition. He says the theater industry is unusual in this way, because...
